---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';

// THE 15-SECOND FIX.
//
// This screen exists because the flow used to route a DJ whose drive mounts
// but shows no playlists straight into formatting a perfectly healthy drive.
// That failure (Device Library vs OneLibrary, see /knowledge/rekordbox) shows
// NO error code, so it looks like a broken drive when nothing is broken. The
// music is still on the stick and FOLDER view plays it right now, with no
// computer and no risk.
---
<Tunnel title="Play from FOLDER view | Save My Gig!" status="Critical · Fastest fix" red>
  <div class="step-label">Try this first, 15 seconds</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Your tracks are probably still there</h2>

  <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">
    Missing playlists usually does not mean a broken drive. The player often
    just cannot read the playlist database, while the music files sit on the
    stick untouched. FOLDER view ignores the database completely.
  </p>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Press <strong>SOURCE</strong> and select your USB.</li>
    <li>Press the <strong>browse / FOLDER</strong> button (on CDJ-2000 and 3000 it is next to the rotary selector).</li>
    <li>Browse the folders on the drive the way you would on a computer.</li>
    <li>Load a track. If it plays, you are back on.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="alert-card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">💡</div>
    <div>
      You lose cues, grids, playlists, Sync and Quantize. You keep the gig.
      Fix the database properly tomorrow, not now.
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="question">Can you load and play a track this way?</p>

  <Choice step="folder_view"
    a={{ href: '/saved?path=critical&branch=folder_view', label: 'YES - TRACKS ARE PLAYING', event: 'outcome_reached', data: { outcome: 'saved', path: 'critical' } }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/critical/have-computer', label: 'NO - STILL NOTHING', desc: 'Then we look at the drive itself.' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
